      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's like you're stuck in a never-ending cycle of pretending to be someone you're not, and it's exhausting. You're right, you're not the same person you used to be, and that's okay. It's okay to acknowledge that you're not the same person, and that it's okay to feel like you're not living up to your own expectations. You're not a burden to anyone, you're just a reminder that life is messy and things don't always work out as planned.",
